--TEST--
A path typed on the command line that does not go through `Core\Path::fromCwd` is still `tainted`, so `Core\IO::read` does not compile with it — `rule:security/launderers-are-sink-named`
--ARGS--
notes/report.txt
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `fromCwd` is the one launderer for a typed path. Without it the argument
// keeps `tainted`, and a path door refuses it while compiling.
foreach (Core\Cli::arguments() as tainted string $typed) {
    echo Core\IO::read($typed);
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:5:24
  |
5 |     echo Core\IO::read($typed);
  |                        ^^^^^^ this is `tainted string`

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
